PHASE 3 — READ-PATH SECURITY CLEARANCE
======================================

Audit every READ path.

Do not assume retrieval is the only path.

Inspect:

* MemoryManagerService
* RetrievalService
* ContextIntegrationService
* MemoryContextProviderAdapter
* consolidation candidate reads
* orchestration memory reads
* repository access where appropriate

Verify that a caller with insufficient security clearance cannot obtain a memory through an alternate path.

Security levels must be enforced consistently.

Required behavior:

LOW clearance cannot access higher-level memory.

INTERNAL cannot access CONFIDENTIAL unless explicitly authorized by the existing policy.

CONFIDENTIAL can access allowed lower levels according to the existing policy.

Do NOT invent a new security model.

Reuse the existing:

* MemoryActor
* securityClearance
* AuthorizationService
* SecurityLevelPolicy
* existing permission matrix
* namespace/ownership policies

Fail closed on:

* missing actor
* invalid actor context
* missing clearance
* malformed security level
* unknown security level

Add regression tests for direct reads and retrieval/context paths.

